Slide 11 — retries, timeouts, circuit breakers and bulkheads
These patterns address different failure modes and should not be treated as interchangeable.

📘 RESILIENCE MECHANISMS — API GATEWAY HLD

🔹 MECHANISM: Timeout / Deadline
🎯 Primary Purpose: Bound how long work may consume resources.
⚠️ Common Mistake: Allowing every downstream call a fresh,
                    excessive timeout.

🔹 MECHANISM: Retry
🎯 Primary Purpose: Recover from transient failures.
⚠️ Common Mistake: Retrying non-idempotent operations without
                    safeguards.

🔹 MECHANISM: Circuit Breaker
🎯 Primary Purpose: Stop repeatedly calling an unhealthy dependency.
⚠️ Common Mistake: Treating it as a substitute for timeouts.

🔹 MECHANISM: Bulkhead
🎯 Primary Purpose: Isolate resource consumption.
⚠️ Common Mistake: Sharing one saturated resource pool across
                    unrelated workloads.

🔹 MECHANISM: Concurrency Limit
🎯 Primary Purpose: Bound simultaneous work.
⚠️ Common Mistake: Choosing a limit without measuring service capacity.

🔹 MECHANISM: Load Shedding
🎯 Primary Purpose: Reject excess work before overload becomes systemic.
⚠️ Common Mistake: Returning success when work was actually discarded.

